+                        // Access pattern: A[i][k] (row-major, good locality for i)
+                        // B[k][j] (column access, bad locality)
+                        // C[i][j] (write)
+                        // Tiling helps reuse A[i][k] across different j's, but B[k][j] remains a bottleneck unless we tile B as well.
+                        // Since we are targeting ARM/NEON, we stick to the structure but apply tiling to reduce outer loop overhead and improve temporal locality for A.
+                        sum += A[i * n + k] * B[k * n + j];
